        ['A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly to 10 m/s in 5 s. It travels at this speed for 10 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 10 s. (a) Sketch the velocity–time graph. (b) Find the acceleration and the deceleration. (c) Find the total distance travelled. (d) Find the average speed for the journey.', ['Graph shape', 'Acceleration', 'Deceleration', 'Distance 175 m', 'Average speed'], '(a) A trapezium: a straight line from (0, 0) up to 10 m/s at 5 s, horizontal until 15 s, then down to zero at 25 s. (b) Acceleration = 10 ÷ 5 = 2 m/s²; deceleration = 10 ÷ 10 = 1 m/s². (c) Distance = area = ½ × 5 × 10 + 10 × 10 + ½ × 10 × 10 = 175 m. (d) Average speed = 175 ÷ 25 = 7 m/s.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly to 30 m/s in 5 s. It travels at this speed for 20 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 5 s. (a) Sketch the velocity–time graph. (b) Find the acceleration and the deceleration. (c) Find the total distance travelled. (d) Find the average speed for the journey.', ['Graph shape', 'Acceleration', 'Deceleration', 'Distance 750 m', 'Average speed'], '(a) A trapezium: a straight line from (0, 0) up to 30 m/s at 5 s, horizontal until 25 s, then down to zero at 30 s. (b) Acceleration = 30 ÷ 5 = 6 m/s²; deceleration = 30 ÷ 5 = 6 m/s². (c) Distance = area = ½ × 5 × 30 + 20 × 30 + ½ × 5 × 30 = 750 m. (d) Average speed = 750 ÷ 30 = 25 m/s.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly to 15 m/s in 4 s. It travels at this speed for 10 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 8 s. (a) Sketch the velocity–time graph. (b) Find the acceleration and the deceleration. (c) Find the total distance travelled. (d) Find the average speed for the journey.', ['Graph shape', 'Acceleration', 'Deceleration', 'Distance 240 m', 'Average speed'], '(a) A trapezium: a straight line from (0, 0) up to 15 m/s at 4 s, horizontal until 14 s, then down to zero at 22 s. (b) Acceleration = 15 ÷ 4 = 3.75 m/s²; deceleration = 15 ÷ 8 = 1.88 m/s². (c) Distance = area = ½ × 4 × 15 + 10 × 15 + ½ × 8 × 15 = 240 m. (d) Average speed = 240 ÷ 22 = 10.91 m/s.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly to 10 m/s in 6 s. It travels at this speed for 30 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 8 s. (a) Sketch the velocity–time graph. (b) Find the acceleration and the deceleration. (c) Find the total distance travelled. (d) Find the average speed for the journey.', ['Graph shape', 'Acceleration', 'Deceleration', 'Distance 370 m', 'Average speed'], '(a) A trapezium: a straight line from (0, 0) up to 10 m/s at 6 s, horizontal until 36 s, then down to zero at 44 s. (b) Acceleration = 10 ÷ 6 = 1.67 m/s²; deceleration = 10 ÷ 8 = 1.25 m/s². (c) Distance = area = ½ × 6 × 10 + 30 × 10 + ½ × 8 × 10 = 370 m. (d) Average speed = 370 ÷ 44 = 8.41 m/s.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A car starts from rest and accelerates uniformly to 30 m/s in 6 s. It travels at this speed for 20 s, then decelerates uniformly to rest in 5 s. (a) Sketch the velocity–time graph. (b) Find the acceleration and the deceleration. (c) Find the total distance travelled. (d) Find the average speed for the journey.', ['Graph shape', 'Acceleration', 'Deceleration', 'Distance 765 m', 'Average speed'], '(a) A trapezium: a straight line from (0, 0) up to 30 m/s at 6 s, horizontal until 26 s, then down to zero at 31 s. (b) Acceleration = 30 ÷ 6 = 5 m/s²; deceleration = 30 ÷ 5 = 6 m/s². (c) Distance = area = ½ × 6 × 30 + 20 × 30 + ½ × 5 × 30 = 765 m. (d) Average speed = 765 ÷ 31 = 24.68 m/s.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
