        ['A ball A of mass 2 kg moving at 5 m/s hits a stationary ball B of mass 1 kg. After the collision, A moves on at 2 m/s in the same direction. (a) State the principle of conservation of linear momentum. (b) Find the velocity of B after the collision. (c) Calculate the total kinetic energy before and after and state whether the collision is elastic.', ['Principle stated', 'Momentum equation', 'v of B', 'KE before and after', 'Elastic or inelastic'], '(a) When no external force acts on a system, the total linear momentum remains constant. (b) 2 × 5 + 0 = 2 × 2 + 1v, so v = 6 m/s. (c) KE before = ½ × 2 × 5² = 25 J. KE after = ½ × 2 × 2² + ½ × 1 × 6² = 22 J. Kinetic energy is lost, so the collision is inelastic.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A ball A of mass 2 kg moving at 6 m/s hits a stationary ball B of mass 2 kg. After the collision, A moves on at 2 m/s in the same direction. (a) State the principle of conservation of linear momentum. (b) Find the velocity of B after the collision. (c) Calculate the total kinetic energy before and after and state whether the collision is elastic.', ['Principle stated', 'Momentum equation', 'v of B', 'KE before and after', 'Elastic or inelastic'], '(a) When no external force acts on a system, the total linear momentum remains constant. (b) 2 × 6 + 0 = 2 × 2 + 2v, so v = 4 m/s. (c) KE before = ½ × 2 × 6² = 36 J. KE after = ½ × 2 × 2² + ½ × 2 × 4² = 20 J. Kinetic energy is lost, so the collision is inelastic.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A ball A of mass 2 kg moving at 8 m/s hits a stationary ball B of mass 2 kg. After the collision, A moves on at 1 m/s in the same direction. (a) State the principle of conservation of linear momentum. (b) Find the velocity of B after the collision. (c) Calculate the total kinetic energy before and after and state whether the collision is elastic.', ['Principle stated', 'Momentum equation', 'v of B', 'KE before and after', 'Elastic or inelastic'], '(a) When no external force acts on a system, the total linear momentum remains constant. (b) 2 × 8 + 0 = 2 × 1 + 2v, so v = 7 m/s. (c) KE before = ½ × 2 × 8² = 64 J. KE after = ½ × 2 × 1² + ½ × 2 × 7² = 50 J. Kinetic energy is lost, so the collision is inelastic.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A ball A of mass 4 kg moving at 5 m/s hits a stationary ball B of mass 2 kg. After the collision, A moves on at 2 m/s in the same direction. (a) State the principle of conservation of linear momentum. (b) Find the velocity of B after the collision. (c) Calculate the total kinetic energy before and after and state whether the collision is elastic.', ['Principle stated', 'Momentum equation', 'v of B', 'KE before and after', 'Elastic or inelastic'], '(a) When no external force acts on a system, the total linear momentum remains constant. (b) 4 × 5 + 0 = 4 × 2 + 2v, so v = 6 m/s. (c) KE before = ½ × 4 × 5² = 50 J. KE after = ½ × 4 × 2² + ½ × 2 × 6² = 44 J. Kinetic energy is lost, so the collision is inelastic.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
        ['A ball A of mass 4 kg moving at 6 m/s hits a stationary ball B of mass 2 kg. After the collision, A moves on at 2 m/s in the same direction. (a) State the principle of conservation of linear momentum. (b) Find the velocity of B after the collision. (c) Calculate the total kinetic energy before and after and state whether the collision is elastic.', ['Principle stated', 'Momentum equation', 'v of B', 'KE before and after', 'Elastic or inelastic'], '(a) When no external force acts on a system, the total linear momentum remains constant. (b) 4 × 6 + 0 = 4 × 2 + 2v, so v = 8 m/s. (c) KE before = ½ × 4 × 6² = 72 J. KE after = ½ × 4 × 2² + ½ × 2 × 8² = 72 J. Kinetic energy is conserved, so the collision is elastic.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 8],
