        ['A block and tackle pulley system has 5 pulleys and is used to raise a load of 600 N with an effort of 160 N. (a) Draw a labelled diagram. (b) Find the velocity ratio. (c) Find the mechanical advantage. (d) Find the efficiency. (e) Give two reasons why the efficiency is less than 100%.', ['Diagram', 'VR = 5', 'MA = 3.75', 'Efficiency 75.0%', 'Two reasons'], '(a) Upper and lower blocks with the rope passing round each pulley; 5 sections of rope support the lower block; effort applied to the free end. (b) VR = number of supporting rope sections = 5. (c) MA = 600 ÷ 160 = 3.75. (d) Efficiency = 3.75 ÷ 5 × 100 = 75.0%. (e) Work is done against friction in the pulleys; work is done lifting the lower block and the rope.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 10],
        ['A block and tackle pulley system has 3 pulleys and is used to raise a load of 600 N with an effort of 267 N. (a) Draw a labelled diagram. (b) Find the velocity ratio. (c) Find the mechanical advantage. (d) Find the efficiency. (e) Give two reasons why the efficiency is less than 100%.', ['Diagram', 'VR = 3', 'MA = 2.25', 'Efficiency 74.9%', 'Two reasons'], '(a) Upper and lower blocks with the rope passing round each pulley; 3 sections of rope support the lower block; effort applied to the free end. (b) VR = number of supporting rope sections = 3. (c) MA = 600 ÷ 267 = 2.25. (d) Efficiency = 2.25 ÷ 3 × 100 = 74.9%. (e) Work is done against friction in the pulleys; work is done lifting the lower block and the rope.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 10],
        ['A block and tackle pulley system has 6 pulleys and is used to raise a load of 600 N with an effort of 133 N. (a) Draw a labelled diagram. (b) Find the velocity ratio. (c) Find the mechanical advantage. (d) Find the efficiency. (e) Give two reasons why the efficiency is less than 100%.', ['Diagram', 'VR = 6', 'MA = 4.51', 'Efficiency 75.2%', 'Two reasons'], '(a) Upper and lower blocks with the rope passing round each pulley; 6 sections of rope support the lower block; effort applied to the free end. (b) VR = number of supporting rope sections = 6. (c) MA = 600 ÷ 133 = 4.51. (d) Efficiency = 4.51 ÷ 6 × 100 = 75.2%. (e) Work is done against friction in the pulleys; work is done lifting the lower block and the rope.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 10],
        ['A block and tackle pulley system has 5 pulleys and is used to raise a load of 600 N with an effort of 150 N. (a) Draw a labelled diagram. (b) Find the velocity ratio. (c) Find the mechanical advantage. (d) Find the efficiency. (e) Give two reasons why the efficiency is less than 100%.', ['Diagram', 'VR = 5', 'MA = 4.00', 'Efficiency 80.0%', 'Two reasons'], '(a) Upper and lower blocks with the rope passing round each pulley; 5 sections of rope support the lower block; effort applied to the free end. (b) VR = number of supporting rope sections = 5. (c) MA = 600 ÷ 150 = 4.00. (d) Efficiency = 4.00 ÷ 5 × 100 = 80.0%. (e) Work is done against friction in the pulleys; work is done lifting the lower block and the rope.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 10],
        ['A block and tackle pulley system has 3 pulleys and is used to raise a load of 600 N with an effort of 250 N. (a) Draw a labelled diagram. (b) Find the velocity ratio. (c) Find the mechanical advantage. (d) Find the efficiency. (e) Give two reasons why the efficiency is less than 100%.', ['Diagram', 'VR = 3', 'MA = 2.40', 'Efficiency 80.0%', 'Two reasons'], '(a) Upper and lower blocks with the rope passing round each pulley; 3 sections of rope support the lower block; effort applied to the free end. (b) VR = number of supporting rope sections = 3. (c) MA = 600 ÷ 250 = 2.40. (d) Efficiency = 2.40 ÷ 3 × 100 = 80.0%. (e) Work is done against friction in the pulleys; work is done lifting the lower block and the rope.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 4, 'theory', 10],
