        ['A football is kicked at 20 m/s at 53° to the horizontal. (g = 10 m/s²) Calculate (a) the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, (b) the time to reach maximum height, (c) the maximum height, (d) the time of flight, (e) the horizontal range.', ['Components', 'Time to top', 'Max height', 'Time of flight', 'Range'], '(a) uₓ = 20 cos 53° = 12.04 m/s; u_y = 20 sin 53° = 15.97 m/s. (b) t = u_y ÷ g = 1.60 s. (c) H = u_y² ÷ 2g = 12.76 m. (d) T = 2 × 1.60 = 3.19 s. (e) R = uₓ × T = 12.04 × 3.19 = 38.45 m.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A football is kicked at 40 m/s at 60° to the horizontal. (g = 10 m/s²) Calculate (a) the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, (b) the time to reach maximum height, (c) the maximum height, (d) the time of flight, (e) the horizontal range.', ['Components', 'Time to top', 'Max height', 'Time of flight', 'Range'], '(a) uₓ = 40 cos 60° = 20.00 m/s; u_y = 40 sin 60° = 34.64 m/s. (b) t = u_y ÷ g = 3.46 s. (c) H = u_y² ÷ 2g = 60.00 m. (d) T = 2 × 3.46 = 6.93 s. (e) R = uₓ × T = 20.00 × 6.93 = 138.56 m.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A football is kicked at 30 m/s at 37° to the horizontal. (g = 10 m/s²) Calculate (a) the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, (b) the time to reach maximum height, (c) the maximum height, (d) the time of flight, (e) the horizontal range.', ['Components', 'Time to top', 'Max height', 'Time of flight', 'Range'], '(a) uₓ = 30 cos 37° = 23.96 m/s; u_y = 30 sin 37° = 18.05 m/s. (b) t = u_y ÷ g = 1.81 s. (c) H = u_y² ÷ 2g = 16.30 m. (d) T = 2 × 1.81 = 3.61 s. (e) R = uₓ × T = 23.96 × 3.61 = 86.51 m.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A football is kicked at 20 m/s at 60° to the horizontal. (g = 10 m/s²) Calculate (a) the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, (b) the time to reach maximum height, (c) the maximum height, (d) the time of flight, (e) the horizontal range.', ['Components', 'Time to top', 'Max height', 'Time of flight', 'Range'], '(a) uₓ = 20 cos 60° = 10.00 m/s; u_y = 20 sin 60° = 17.32 m/s. (b) t = u_y ÷ g = 1.73 s. (c) H = u_y² ÷ 2g = 15.00 m. (d) T = 2 × 1.73 = 3.46 s. (e) R = uₓ × T = 10.00 × 3.46 = 34.64 m.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A football is kicked at 30 m/s at 53° to the horizontal. (g = 10 m/s²) Calculate (a) the horizontal and vertical components of the initial velocity, (b) the time to reach maximum height, (c) the maximum height, (d) the time of flight, (e) the horizontal range.', ['Components', 'Time to top', 'Max height', 'Time of flight', 'Range'], '(a) uₓ = 30 cos 53° = 18.05 m/s; u_y = 30 sin 53° = 23.96 m/s. (b) t = u_y ÷ g = 2.40 s. (c) H = u_y² ÷ 2g = 28.70 m. (d) T = 2 × 2.40 = 4.79 s. (e) R = uₓ × T = 18.05 × 4.79 = 86.51 m.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
