        ['Centripetal force is', ['an outward force', 'zero', 'the resultant force towards the centre that keeps a body in circular motion', 'the weight of the body only'], 'C', 'F = mv²/r.', 2],
        ['Centripetal acceleration is given by', ['vr', 'v/r²', 'r/v²', 'v²/r'], 'D', 'Also ω²r.', 2],
        ['Angular velocity ω is related to linear speed v by', ['v = ωr', 'v = ω/r', 'v = r/ω', 'v = ω²r'], 'A', 'Unit rad/s.', 2],
        ['If the string of a whirling stone breaks, the stone moves', ['towards the centre', 'along the tangent to the circle', 'outwards along the radius', 'in a spiral'], 'B', 'Newton\'s first law.', 2],
        ['For a car turning on a flat road, the centripetal force is provided by', ['the engine', 'gravity alone', 'friction between the tyres and the road', 'air resistance'], 'C', 'Too little friction causes skidding.', 3],
        ['Newton\'s law of universal gravitation states that the force between two masses is', ['proportional to distance', 'independent of mass', 'proportional to the sum of masses', 'proportional to the product of their masses and inversely proportional to the square of their distance'], 'D', 'F = Gm₁m₂/r².', 3],
        ['The value of the universal gravitational constant G is about', ['6.67 × 10⁻¹¹ N m² kg⁻²', '9.8 N/kg', '3 × 10⁸ m/s', '1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ C'], 'A', 'Very small.', 3],
        ['The acceleration due to gravity on the Moon is about', ['six times that on Earth', 'one-sixth of that on Earth', 'the same as on Earth', 'zero'], 'B', 'About 1.6 m/s².', 2],
        ['A geostationary satellite has a period of', ['1 hour', '12 hours', '24 hours', '365 days'], 'C', 'It stays above one point on the equator.', 3],
        ['The centripetal force for a satellite orbiting the Earth is provided by', ['friction', 'its engines', 'air resistance', 'gravitational attraction'], 'D', 'Weight provides it.', 2],
        ['Escape velocity from the Earth\'s surface is about', ['11.2 km/s', '3 × 10⁸ m/s', '340 m/s', '1 km/s'], 'A', 'v = √(2gR).', 4],
        ['A body moves in a circle of radius 50 m at 10 m/s. Find its angular velocity.', ['500 rad/s', '0.2 rad/s', '5 rad/s', '2 rad/s'], 'B', 'ω = v ÷ r.', 2],
        ['A wheel makes 3 revolutions in 1 s. Find its period.', ['3 s', '18.85 s', '0.333 s', '1.333 s'], 'C', 'T = time ÷ revolutions.', 2],
        ['A wheel makes 2 revolutions in 1 s. Find its period.', ['2 s', '12.57 s', '1.5 s', '0.5 s'], 'D', 'T = time ÷ revolutions.', 2],
        ['A body moves in a circle of radius 5 m at 10 m/s. Find its angular velocity.', ['2 rad/s', '50 rad/s', '0.5 rad/s', '20 rad/s'], 'A', 'ω = v ÷ r.', 2],
        ['A 1 kg mass moves in a circle of radius 1 m at 5 m/s. Find the centripetal force.', ['5 N', '25 N', '12.5 N', '26 N'], 'B', 'F = mv² ÷ r.', 3],
        ['A 0.5 kg mass moves in a circle of radius 5 m at 2 m/s. Find the centripetal force.', ['0.2 N', '10 N', '0.4 N', '1.4 N'], 'C', 'F = mv² ÷ r.', 3],
        ['A 1 kg mass moves in a circle of radius 50 m at 2 m/s. Find the centripetal force.', ['0.04 N', '200 N', '1.08 N', '0.08 N'], 'D', 'F = mv² ÷ r.', 3],
        ['A wheel makes 4 revolutions in 2 s. Find its period.', ['0.5 s', '2 s', '8 s', '12.57 s'], 'A', 'T = time ÷ revolutions.', 2],
        ['A body moving in a circle at constant speed is accelerating.', ['True', 'False'], 'A', 'Its velocity direction changes.', 2, 'tf'],
        ['Centrifugal force is the real force that keeps a body in circular motion.', ['True', 'False'], 'B', 'The real inward force is centripetal.', 3, 'tf'],
        ['Doubling the distance between two masses reduces the gravitational force to one quarter.', ['True', 'False'], 'A', 'Inverse square law.', 2, 'tf'],
        ['Astronauts in orbit feel weightless because there is no gravity there.', ['True', 'False'], 'B', 'They are in free fall; gravity still acts.', 4, 'tf'],
        ['Banking a road helps vehicles take bends safely at higher speeds.', ['True', 'False'], 'A', 'Part of the normal reaction gives centripetal force.', 3, 'tf'],
        ['Communication satellites are often geostationary.', ['True', 'False'], 'A', 'Fixed position relative to Earth.', 2, 'tf'],
        ['The centripetal acceleration of a body moving at 3 m/s in a circle of radius 1 m is ___ m/s².', ['9'], '', 'a = v² ÷ r.', 2, 'fill'],
