        ['A series circuit contains a resistor of 40 Ω, an inductor of reactance 80 Ω and a capacitor of reactance 60 Ω, connected to a 100 V r.m.s. a.c. supply. Calculate (a) the impedance, (b) the r.m.s. current, (c) the p.d. across each component, (d) the phase angle between current and supply voltage.', ['Impedance', 'Current', 'Component p.d.s', 'Phase angle'], '(a) Z = √(40² + (80 − 60)²) = 44.72 Ω. (b) I = 100 ÷ 44.72 = 2.24 A. (c) V_R = 2.24 × 40 = 89.6 V; V_L = 2.24 × 80 = 179.2 V; V_C = 2.24 × 60 = 134.4 V. (d) tan φ = (80 − 60) ÷ 40, so φ = 26.6°, with the current lagging the voltage.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A series circuit contains a resistor of 30 Ω, an inductor of reactance 120 Ω and a capacitor of reactance 60 Ω, connected to a 240 V r.m.s. a.c. supply. Calculate (a) the impedance, (b) the r.m.s. current, (c) the p.d. across each component, (d) the phase angle between current and supply voltage.', ['Impedance', 'Current', 'Component p.d.s', 'Phase angle'], '(a) Z = √(30² + (120 − 60)²) = 67.08 Ω. (b) I = 240 ÷ 67.08 = 3.58 A. (c) V_R = 3.58 × 30 = 107.4 V; V_L = 3.58 × 120 = 429.6 V; V_C = 3.58 × 60 = 214.8 V. (d) tan φ = (120 − 60) ÷ 30, so φ = 63.4°, with the current lagging the voltage.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A series circuit contains a resistor of 30 Ω, an inductor of reactance 100 Ω and a capacitor of reactance 40 Ω, connected to a 100 V r.m.s. a.c. supply. Calculate (a) the impedance, (b) the r.m.s. current, (c) the p.d. across each component, (d) the phase angle between current and supply voltage.', ['Impedance', 'Current', 'Component p.d.s', 'Phase angle'], '(a) Z = √(30² + (100 − 40)²) = 67.08 Ω. (b) I = 100 ÷ 67.08 = 1.49 A. (c) V_R = 1.49 × 30 = 44.7 V; V_L = 1.49 × 100 = 149.0 V; V_C = 1.49 × 40 = 59.6 V. (d) tan φ = (100 − 40) ÷ 30, so φ = 63.4°, with the current lagging the voltage.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A series circuit contains a resistor of 60 Ω, an inductor of reactance 100 Ω and a capacitor of reactance 40 Ω, connected to a 200 V r.m.s. a.c. supply. Calculate (a) the impedance, (b) the r.m.s. current, (c) the p.d. across each component, (d) the phase angle between current and supply voltage.', ['Impedance', 'Current', 'Component p.d.s', 'Phase angle'], '(a) Z = √(60² + (100 − 40)²) = 84.85 Ω. (b) I = 200 ÷ 84.85 = 2.36 A. (c) V_R = 2.36 × 60 = 141.6 V; V_L = 2.36 × 100 = 236.0 V; V_C = 2.36 × 40 = 94.4 V. (d) tan φ = (100 − 40) ÷ 60, so φ = 45.0°, with the current lagging the voltage.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['A series circuit contains a resistor of 40 Ω, an inductor of reactance 100 Ω and a capacitor of reactance 40 Ω, connected to a 240 V r.m.s. a.c. supply. Calculate (a) the impedance, (b) the r.m.s. current, (c) the p.d. across each component, (d) the phase angle between current and supply voltage.', ['Impedance', 'Current', 'Component p.d.s', 'Phase angle'], '(a) Z = √(40² + (100 − 40)²) = 72.11 Ω. (b) I = 240 ÷ 72.11 = 3.33 A. (c) V_R = 3.33 × 40 = 133.2 V; V_L = 3.33 × 100 = 333.0 V; V_C = 3.33 × 40 = 133.2 V. (d) tan φ = (100 − 40) ÷ 40, so φ = 56.3°, with the current lagging the voltage.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
