        ['Ultraviolet light of wavelength 300 nm falls on a metal surface of work function 2 eV. (h = 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s, 1 eV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J) Calculate (a) the energy of each photon in joules and in eV, (b) the maximum kinetic energy of the emitted electrons in eV, (c) the threshold frequency of the metal. (d) State the effect of doubling the intensity of the light.', ['Photon energy J', 'Photon energy eV', 'KE_max', 'Threshold frequency', 'Intensity effect'], '(a) E = hc ÷ λ = 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3 × 10⁸ ÷ 300 × 10⁻⁹ = 6.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J = 4.13 eV. (b) KE_max = 4.13 − 2 = 2.13 eV. (c) f₀ = φ ÷ h = 2 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ = 4.85 × 10¹⁴ Hz. (d) Twice as many electrons are emitted per second, but their maximum kinetic energy is unchanged.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
        ['Ultraviolet light of wavelength 350 nm falls on a metal surface of work function 2 eV. (h = 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ J s, c = 3 × 10⁸ m/s, 1 eV = 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ J) Calculate (a) the energy of each photon in joules and in eV, (b) the maximum kinetic energy of the emitted electrons in eV, (c) the threshold frequency of the metal. (d) State the effect of doubling the intensity of the light.', ['Photon energy J', 'Photon energy eV', 'KE_max', 'Threshold frequency', 'Intensity effect'], '(a) E = hc ÷ λ = 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ × 3 × 10⁸ ÷ 350 × 10⁻⁹ = 5.66 × 10⁻¹⁹ J = 3.54 eV. (b) KE_max = 3.54 − 2 = 1.54 eV. (c) f₀ = φ ÷ h = 2 × 1.6 × 10⁻¹⁹ ÷ 6.6 × 10⁻³⁴ = 4.85 × 10¹⁴ Hz. (d) Twice as many electrons are emitted per second, but their maximum kinetic energy is unchanged.', 'Compare your answer with the model answer and tick off the points you made.', 5, 'theory', 10],
