        ['Water is a poor conductor of heat. This can be shown by', ['heating a metal rod', 'shining light on it', 'boiling water at the top of a tube while ice at the bottom stays frozen', 'freezing it'], 'C', 'Ice weighted down with gauze.', 3],
        ['The heating element of an electric kettle is placed at the bottom so that', ['it is safer', 'it uses less power', 'radiation is reduced', 'convection currents heat all the water'], 'D', 'Hot water rises.', 2],
        ['Cooking pots often have wooden or plastic handles because these are', ['poor conductors (insulators)', 'good conductors', 'shiny', 'heavy'], 'A', 'They stay cool.', 1],
        ['Houses in hot climates are often painted white because white surfaces', ['absorb radiant heat', 'reflect radiant heat', 'conduct heat well', 'cause convection'], 'B', 'Keeps rooms cooler.', 1],
        ['The greenhouse effect in a glasshouse occurs because glass', ['blocks all radiation', 'conducts heat very well', 'lets short-wave radiation in but traps long-wave infrared', 'reflects all light'], 'C', 'Plants and soil re-emit long waves.', 4],
